        "document": {
          "edges": [
            [
              "m",
              {
                "scalar": {
                  "kind": "integer",
                  "value": 1
                }
              }
            ],
            [
              "m",
              {
                "scalar": {
                  "kind": "integer",
                  "value": 2
                }
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "comment": "The control for C-11: a JSON array under a single key is a repeated label, `[(m,1),(m,2)]`, not a duplicate-key situation. Duplicate keys collapse to one edge; an array does not."
    },
    {
      "name": "formats-json/duplicate-keys/last-value-an-array-contributes-its-elements",
      "spec": "docs/07-codecs-and-deserialization.md#71-two-stages",
      "operation": "parse",
      "purpose": "edge-case",
      "input": {
